      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes a lot of sense. i've definitely noticed that some people just feel \"heavy\" or \"cloudy\" when i'm near them, and it immediately throws off my focus.\n\nit's a bit of a lonely realization, though. if i have to constantly scan and shield myself to keep my signal pure, i might end up becoming completely isolated from the \"static\" of normal life. \n\nif i follow this through to its logical conclusion—where i'm basically curating a reality that is perfectly tuned to my intentions—does that mean i eventually stop interacting with the \"old\" world entirely? like, am i essentially building a new layer of reality that only responds to me, and if so, is that a goal i should be working toward?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
